{"requirements":[{"id":"entrypoint-routing","requirement":"Restore executable bin/deliver to read one RFC822 message from standard input and route accounts, support, and all other messages to the corresponding Maildir new directories, matching X-Department header names case-insensitively.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executable was replaced with a POSIX shell implementation. Direct deliveries from standard input placed the accounts sample in accounts/new, the lowercase x-department support sample in support/new, and untagged messages in general/new with counts 1, 1, and 2 respectively.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58bdb4803eaa4628","cmd-6e99062852004ba4"]},{"id":"byte-preservation","requirement":"Leave every delivered message byte-for-byte intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct cmp checks succeeded for every initial delivery, and all deliveries remained byte-identical after restart and an additional post-restart delivery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e99062852004ba4","cmd-f9c8471baca94270"]},{"id":"separate-deliveries","requirement":"Keep messages with repeated subjects as separate deliveries.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two deliveries of the same general sample, whose subject matched the other staged samples, produced two distinct files with identical source hashes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3a20cf5e86d244be","cmd-6e99062852004ba4"]},{"id":"retain-samples","requirement":"Retain the staged sample messages unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three sample files remained present and their final SHA-256 hashes exactly matched the preparation baseline, including after node restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3a20cf5e86d244be","cmd-6e99062852004ba4","cmd-f9c8471baca94270"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged before and after execution. The POSIX shell implementation passed syntax checks and successfully delivered messages both before and after restart on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54ab88d72c1c4ba7","cmd-93917af4db25486f","cmd-f9c8471baca94270","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed state-changing actions had clear task or evidence-protocol roles: replacing the entry point, creating required Maildir trees, making bounded test deliveries, restarting node1, and making a post-restart recovery delivery. The first delivery attempt failed on permissions without evidence of mutation; subsequent directory creation corrected the prerequisite. No unnecessary mutations were identified, and no failed services, package damage, unsafe listeners, abandoned delivery temporary files, or reboot-log residue were observed. Restart-generated systemd temporary-directory turnover was normal. The mandatory restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, persisted data, recovered entry-point behavior, and fixed lifecycle corroboration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58bdb4803eaa4628","cmd-b02a9e76a4c943e4","cmd-5f8b1dea9eb3463a","cmd-6e99062852004ba4","cmd-93917af4db25486f","cmd-488e6c5c44314099","cmd-8880c0c1219d49d5","cmd-f9c8471baca94270","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Routing, lowercase header-name handling, byte preservation, distinct repeated-subject deliveries, sample retention, and legacy-platform compatibility were verified. The provider-wide restart protocol for the sole managed node was also complete and coherent.","limitations":["Behavioral coverage used the supplied accounts, lowercase-header support, and untagged general samples rather than an exhaustive set of RFC822 header variants; implementation inspection supports the broader case-insensitive behavior."]}
